{"step_index":538,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T06:42:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-04T00:42:26-06:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-04T00:42:28-06:00\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n# ==============================================================================\r\n# CONFIGURACIÓN DE ENTORNO U-BOOT (env) — ZTE ZXV10 B866V2 (Placa: franklin / g12a)\r\n# Procesador: Amlogic S905X2 | Memoria: 2GB DDR4 + 8GB eMMC | Wi-Fi: MT7661LSN\r\n# ==============================================================================\r\n\r\nbaudrate=115200\r\nboard=franklin\r\nsoc=g12a\r\narch=arm\r\ncpu=armv8\r\n\r\n# Parámetros de salida de video HDMI y espacio de color (Amlogic VOUT / HDMITX)\r\nhdmimode=1080p60hz\r\noutputmode=1080p60hz\r\ncolorattribute=444,8bit\r\ndolby_status=0\r\nhdr_policy=1\r\nfrac_rate_policy=1\r\n\r\n# Resolución del Framebuffer de interfaz (OSD)\r\nfb_width=1920\r\nfb_height=1080\r\ndisplay_bpp=32\r\ndisplay_color_index=32\r\ndisplay_layer=osd0\r\n\r\n# Argumentos pasados al Kernel Linux (cmdline)\r\ninitargs=rootfstype=ramfs init=/init console=ttyS0,115200 no_console_suspend earlycon=aml-uart,0xff803000 ramoops.pstore_en=1 ramoops.record_size=0x8000 ramoops.console_size=0x4000\r\n\r\n# Comandos de arranque estándar (Android 12 en eMMC)\r\nstoreboot=imgread kernel boot ${loadaddr}; bootm ${loadaddr};\r\n\r\n# Configuración de Multiboot por USB / SD (Armbian / Debian / CoreELEC / EmuELEC)\r\n# Basado en mirko-geno/b866v2-debian y ophub/amlogic-s9xxx-armbian\r\nstart_autoscript=if usb start; then run start_usb_autoscript; fi; if mmcinfo; then run start_mmc_autoscript; fi;\r\nstart_usb_autoscript=if fatload usb 0 1020000 s905_autoscript; then autoscr 1020000; fi; if fatload usb 1 1020000 s905_autoscript; then autoscr 1020000; fi;\r\nstart_mmc_autoscript=if fatload mmc 0 1020000 s905_autoscript; then autoscr 1020000; fi;\r\n"}
{"step_index":539,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-04T06:42:28Z","input_tokens":2927,"cache_read_tokens":216148,"output_tokens":2086,"thinking":"The log indicates a potential upgrade sequence being triggered. The mention of \"active slot = 0\" and an \"integer compare\" suggests a check or validation during this process. This observation requires further investigation to determine if it is relevant to the current problem.\n\n\nThe \"detect upgrade key\" message is directly tied to the `itest` command's behavior within the U-Boot environment. The `itest` command, due to an undefined environment variable (`upgrade_key_flag`), results in an unexpected argument count, leading to its usage message and a false return value, preventing the update sequence from triggering. Further investigation is needed to verify this hypothesis by comparing with an older U-Boot version where the update is successful.\n\n\nThe older U-Boot version's behavior shows that holding RESET (GPIOAO_3 == 0) triggers the upgrade key detection, then the `itest` command with the undefined variable leads to the usage message. This condition, leading to the \"itest\" command failing, prevents the update sequence. This aligns with the boot logs observed where the kernel later restarts the system with the 'recovery' command.\n\n\nThe newer U-Boot version (Sep 05 2023) does not enter the USB burn mode when RESET is held. Instead, it triggers a kernel reboot into recovery or fastbootd based on USB content. The \"StartDedicatedWorldCupHuntFromLockedFastboot\" failure on the user's test case is now understood: the instructions given were for the 2021 U-Boot, not the Sep 05 2023 version where the key check is broken. The critical question now is how a locked device with the newer U-Boot can be unlocked externally.\n\n\nThe focus shifts to exploring potential vulnerabilities in `fastbootd` (PID_4EE7), Recovery, and Android to unlock the locked device. A test device entered `fastbootd` (PID_4EE7) after holding RESET while a USB drive with `factory_update_param.aml` was inserted. The immediate jump to U-Boot Fastboot (PID_0D02) after the detection of `fastbootd` prompts further investigation into the functionalities of `fastbootd` prior to the transition. The next step will involve examining the `fastbootd` and `recovery` binaries for available commands and attack vectors.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"$bytes = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes(\"c:\\Users\\andre\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\xview\\experimento\\11_VALIDACION_OTA_Y_FIRMWARE_ZTE\\system_bin_recovery\")\n$ascii = [System.Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetString($bytes)\n[regex]::Matches($ascii, \"[ -~]{8,}\") | ForEach-Object { $_.Value } | Where-Object { $_ -match \"fastboot|udisk|factory_update|ubootenv|otg_device|lock|oem|flashing|last_QR|adb\" } | Select-Object -First 80","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Search system_bin_recovery for fastboot, udisk, ubootenv, and lock strings"}}]}
